{"type":"assistant","uuid":"477e2bd3-2cca-4529-be4e-9d67b03a4068","session_id":"c9e96794-fa97-493f-aec3-2e476494fcd8","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"477e2bd3-2cca-4529-be4e-9d67b03a4068","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is complete and verified. Here's a summary:\n\n---\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**Bug**: Entering `9999` as the TOTP code refresh time causes Aegis to crash instantly.\n\n**Root Cause — Division by Zero in `TotpProgressBar.refresh()`**:\n```java\n// In TotpProgressBar.java, line ~68\nint animPart = maxProgress / _period;  // 5000 / 9999 = 0 (integer division)\nint animEnd = (currentProgress / animPart) * animPart;  // DIVISION BY ZERO!\n```\n\nWhen `_period` exceeds `maxProgress` (5000), integer division yields 0, causing an `ArithmeticException` crash.\n\n**Fix — Two layers of defense:**\n\n1. **`TotpInfo.java`** — Tightened `isPeriodValid()` to reject periods > 5000 seconds (practical upper bound for the progress bar).\n\n2. **`TotpProgressBar.java`** — Added a defensive guard in `refresh()` that bypasses the animation logic when `_period > maxProgress`, simply setting progress directly.\n\n**Files modified**:\n- `app/src/main/java/com/beemdevelopment/aegis/otp/TotpInfo.java`\n- `app/src/main/java/com/beemdevelopment/aegis/ui/views/TotpProgressBar.java`\n\n**Build**: Compiles successfully — `BUILD SUCCESSFUL`.\n\nThe patch has been saved to `fix.patch`."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":51974,"output_tokens":549,"cache_read_input_tokens":17952,"total_tokens":52523}}}
